From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP requestPartition must accept region 0

Spawn is Folia region id 0. requestPartition treated 0 as unset, so a
finished packed-spawn carve logged "partition requested" and never
enqueued tryForcePartition — no "into 2 shards". Hot streak still puts
region 0 in PARTITION_REQUESTS (that is how carve started). Same class
of bug as the in-flight cut key. Log when the post-carve groups are not
spatially buffered instead of silent requeue. Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/YapSubRegionPartitioner.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/YapSubRegionPartitioner.java
@@ -93,8 +93,11 @@
     }
 
     public static void requestPartition(final long regionId, final int shardCount) {
-        if (!ENABLED || regionId == 0L) {
+        if (!ENABLED) {
             return;
         }
+        // Region 0 is the overworld spawn blob. Treating 0 as "unset" dropped the
+        // post-carve retry, so packed spawn emptied the hole and never into-shards.
         PARTITION_REQUESTS.put(regionId, Math.min(4, Math.max(2, shardCount)));
     }
 
@@ -242,6 +245,8 @@
                 return false;
             }
             if (YapCorridorCarver.recentlyCarved(region.id)) {
+                LOGGER.info("YaP force-partition deferred region #{} — carve done but shards not spatially buffered (not into-shards)",
+                        region.id);
                 PARTITION_REQUESTS.put(region.id, Math.min(4, Math.max(2, shardCount)));
                 return false;
             }
